{
 "id": "025-gunaydin-iyi-geceler",
 "lang": "en",
 "title": "Good Morning, Good Night",
 "theme": "Greetings for the time of day",
 "blurb": "Sleepy Ali blurts out “Good night!” to his neighbour Granny Nazlı one morning and feels embarrassed. With Grandpa's secret, he finds the right greeting all day long: Look at the sky, find the greeting!",
 "voiceNames": {
  "ali": "Ali",
  "dede": "Grandpa (Ali's grandpa)",
  "nine": "Granny Nazlı (neighbour)",
  "nur": "Miss Nur",
  "aylin": "Dr Aylin (neighbour)",
  "boncuk": "Buttons (Ali's dog)"
 },
 "pages": [
  {
   "text": "Morning came and the sun rose. Ali's eyes were still sleepy. He went out into the street with Grandpa and his dog Buttons. “Good morning, Ali!” said Granny Nazlı. Out it popped from Ali's mouth: “Good night!”",
   "hits": {
    "gunes": {
     "say": "The sun has just risen, low in the sky. Good morning time!"
    },
    "ali": {
     "say": "Good night, Granny Nazlı!"
    },
    "nine": {
     "say": "Good morning, Ali! Good morning, Buttons!"
    },
    "dede": {
     "say": "Good morning, Nazlı!"
    },
    "boncuk": {
     "say": "Woof! Woof in the morning, woof at night!"
    }
   },
   "hint": "Touch the sun!",
   "ask": "Why did Ali get mixed up? What do we say when we meet someone in the morning?"
  },
  {
   "text": "“Good night?” said Granny. “I've only just woken up!” Ali felt embarrassed. His cheeks went warm. He hid behind Grandpa. Granny smiled: “Good morning, Buttons! Good morning, Ali!”",
   "hits": {
    "ali": {
     "say": "I got mixed up… My cheeks are warm."
    },
    "nine": {
     "say": "That happens, sweetheart. Good morning!"
    },
    "dede": {
     "say": "It's okay to feel shy, Ali. I'm right here."
    },
    "boncuk": {
     "say": "Woof! Woof!"
    }
   },
   "hint": "Touch Ali!",
   "ask": "Why did Ali hide? What do you do when you feel embarrassed?"
  },
  {
   "text": "At midday they went to the market. Suddenly, Miss Nur appeared! Ali's heart went thump, thump. Grandpa whispered: “Look at the sky, find the greeting!”",
   "hits": {
